# ============================================================
# Save this as  .gitignore  in the repo root  (~/projects/NRG/.gitignore)
# ============================================================

# --- Python environment (never commit) ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Private master spreadsheet (full version) — but KEEP the pipeline ODS ---
*.ods
!Newborough_well_records_pipeline.ods

# --- Local work notes (not for publishing) ---

# --- Water Watch newsletters (Google Drive + Facebook, not git) ---
Living_output/
living/output/
*Water_Watch*.pdf

# --- LibreOffice lock files ---
.~lock.*#

# --- Large local working document (189 MB) — keep the PDF, not the docx ---
report.docx
*.odt
*.docx
*.xls*
*.sh
# the gate and the build scripts are source, not generated output
!tools/*.sh
*.tmp

# --- Reference only (frozen-PL chat's call; already-tracked needs git rm --cached) ---
# outputs/**/*.png
outputs/logs/*.log

# --- Living working folders (local only) ---
living/inbox/
living/output/

# --- Report editing sources (report_edits/) ---
# Policy: version the TEXT MIRROR, not the binaries.
#
# The .odt subdocuments and the frozen pre-edit backups are ~200 MB each. They
# are zip archives, so git cannot delta-compress or diff them: every commit
# would store a fresh 200 MB blob, and GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100 MB.
# They are working files, backed up outside the repo (external drive / Drive).
#
# What IS versioned: report_edits/text/*.md (the pandoc mirror — small, diffable,
# equations preserved as LaTeX), CHAPTER_MAP.md, and make_text_mirror.sh.
# Regenerate the mirror after every .odt edit and commit it alongside.
report_edits/odt/

# The three graveyards — _frozen/, backups/, _superseded/ — moved to scratch/
# on 2026-08-27. 888 MB of pre-edit snapshots that had been sitting inside a
# content directory. report_edits/ now holds only the live documents (odt/)
# and their mirrors (text/).
/scratch/
# Pre-edit safety copies of the chapter .odt files, written before any
# automated edit pass. Same size class as the originals — report9 alone is
# 121 MB, over GitHub's hard 100 MB limit — and the same argument applies:
# they are working files, not history. Added 2026-08-20, after seven of
# them were committed by accident and the push was rejected.

# Re-open the blanket *.sh rule for the mirror script only.
!report_edits/*.sh

# The master .odm carries only links and styles, so it is small and safe to
# track. Confirm with `du -h report_edits/report.odm` before the first commit;
# if it is large, ignore it too.
!report_edits/*.odm

# Keep LibreOffice lock/backup cruft out of the tracked folder regardless.
report_edits/**/.~lock.*#
report_edits/**/*.bak
report_edits/**/*~

# Sentinel-watcher auto-push state (runtime only; never versioned).
# Sentinel, logs, result and lock for tools/nrg_push_watch.sh + nrg_autopush.sh.
.nrg_push/

# local trash folder + LibreOffice deleted-but-open relics — never commit
/_to_delete/
.fuse_hidden*

# --- Reference library (store/) — READ LOCALLY, NEVER PUBLISHED ---
# Papers, agency reports and other third-party reference material live here so
# they can be read from the working copy and survive between sessions.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Almost everything that belongs in this folder is
# under publisher or agency copyright — the Journal of Ecology PDFs carry JSTOR
# terms that permit personal, non-commercial use and forbid redistribution — so
# the contents are never committed. Note that PDFs are NOT otherwise ignored by
# this file: without the rule below, anything dropped in here would be tracked
# and pushed on the next run of nrg_git.sh.
#
# The manifest IS tracked, so provenance is versioned without the material being
# republished. Add a row to store/README.md when you add a document.
literature/*
!literature/README.md

# --- Historic map scans — LOCAL ONLY, licence-restricted ---
# Georeferenced scans of third-party historic mapping (OS County Series and the
# like). This repository is public and these scans carry the publisher's or
# host's licence — NLS georeferenced sheets are typically CC-BY-NC-SA — so they
# are never committed, for the same reason as store/.
#
# What IS tracked is the DERIVED geometry digitised from them: coast.kml
# (1899 high tide + dune edge) and DCoast_2015.kml (2015 dune edge) are original
# work and are the evidence base for the retreat measurement, so they belong in
# the repository and the scan does not.
#
# Put any further historic sheets in data/geo/histmaps/ rather than adding a
# rule per file.
data/geo/1900 copy_modified.tif
data/geo/histmaps/

# ── Working records: private by decision, 2026-08-24 ─────────────────────────
# The raw decision log and the changelog deltas are working documents — they
# carry the back-and-forth of the analysis, not its conclusions. What belongs
# in a public repository is the settled decision, which lives in
# DECISIONS_PUBLIC.md and keeps the same D-numbers so existing citations
# resolve. These stay on disk and out of git.
_audit_tmp/
tools/Handover_NRG_rebuild_Cowork.md
tools/NRG_figure_refresh_plan_2026-08-12.md
living/HANDOVER_pipeline_forecaster_regen_2026-07-04.md
docs/papers/paper_2/PAPER2_EDITS.md

# The private working-records repository (see README_WORKING.md)
.git-working/

# NOTE — /working/ and /nrg_git.sh are NOT ignored here, deliberately.
# .gitignore is a working-tree file and BOTH repositories read it, and it
# outranks $GIT_DIR/info/exclude. Naming the private paths here hid them from
# the private repository too, which is the one that is supposed to track them.
# Each repository's exclusion therefore lives in its own git directory:
#     .git/info/exclude          ignores /working/ and /nrg_git.sh
#     .git-working/info/exclude  ignores /* and re-includes exactly those two
# See BOOTSTRAP.md — a fresh clone must be given both.

# Marker touched by nrg_git option 11 on a successful Drive archive
.last_drive_archive

# The documents lock is a working record: it says which MACHINE currently
# holds the ODTs. It belongs to the private repo (WGIT_PATHS carries it) and
# must never reach the public one, where it would be meaningless to a reader
# and would conflict on every push between machines.
